{
 "_source": "The platinum plant's live stages as the pack loads them (GT-- 1.3.10, gtnn-1.20.1-1.3.10.jar pinned in pack/mods/gtnn.pw.toml, and GTM 7.5.3), read from the native recipe dump of the power-quests-1 bench run (2026-10-25, tools/test kubejs-exported/recipes.json, format gg-recipes-1), the same dump as gtnn-1.3.10-naquadah-line.json: the original recipes of every stage of the plant's attack_pentlandite plan (mode 1) and of GT--'s iridium and osmium chain that modes 3 and 4 share (server_scripts/grindless/ev/platinum_plant.js, its PLANS). The other plans' stages are not here (LuV A2, mode 4).",
 "_how_it_is_used": [
  "tools/analysis/test/platinum-asteroid.test.mjs runs server_scripts/grindless/lib/compose.js and ev/platinum_plant.js on these recipes (a stand-in for ServerEvents.recipes' originalRecipes, tools/analysis/lib/kubejs_recipes_sandbox.mjs) and checks mode 4 (circuit 4, asteroid platinum metals) against data/grindless/tables/asteroid_pgm.json and docs/eras/luv.md. The separation plans, whose stages are not pinned, are skipped there.",
  "liveComposed is the plant's attack_pentlandite and iridosmine recipes as the same native run built them: the stand-in must compose exactly those (same contents, EU/t and duration).",
  "related: the Mercury fusion grindless:solar_processing/iridosmine_fusion as that run built it (IV-B2's server_scripts/grindless/iv/mercury.js, from the object it publishes as global.grindless.mercury.fusion): modes 3 and 4 price their first stage from it, and the test checks that the script's object still matches it.",
  "When pack/mods/gtnn.pw.toml moves to another GT-- version the test fails on purpose: dump the new pack natively, rebuild this file from it (same ids) with the new gtnnVersion, and re-check the modes before accepting it."
 ],
